        <title type="html"><![CDATA[chore(dictionaries): add technical terms flagged by spelling check]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43907</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43907"/>
        <updated>2026-04-23T13:38:51.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153818647?u=6905f8dc8a150afb4247652c2da18ab0ce032377&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h2 dir="auto">Summary</h2>
<p dir="auto">Adds the valid technical terms flagged by the automated weekly spelling check (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4292390924" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43850" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43850/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43850">#43850</a>) to the spell-check dictionaries so future scans stop reporting them as unknown words.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Issue</h2>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43850.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4292390924" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43850" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43850/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43850">#43850</a></p>
<p dir="auto">The two actual typos (<code class="notranslate">scrset</code> → <code class="notranslate">srcset</code>, <code class="notranslate">LUNDDUN</code> → <code class="notranslate">LINDDUN</code>) were already corrected in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4293496329" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43852" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/43852/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43852">#43852</a>. This PR handles the remaining items from the same report, all of which are legitimate terms that need to be dictionary-allowed rather than edited out of the content.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Changes</h2>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">.vscode/dictionaries/code-entities.txt</code>:
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">andnot</code> — WebAssembly SIMD bitwise instruction</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">bitselect</code> — WebAssembly SIMD bitwise instruction</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">laneidx</code> — WebAssembly SIMD immediate operand</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">memidx</code> — WebAssembly immediate operand</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">myattr</code> — placeholder attribute name used in the CSS `attr()` namespace example</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>`.vscode/dictionaries/proper-names.txt`:
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">LINDDUN</code> — privacy-focused threat-modeling framework (referenced in `web/security/threat_modeling/`)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Entries were inserted in the existing alphabetical position for each file.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Testing</h2>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Docs-only change; no content files modified.</li>
<li>Ran `grep` to verify each term has at least one occurrence in `files/en-us/` so the dictionary addition is backed by real usage.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
